1
00:00:04,652 --> 00:00:09,492
Lesson five: notifications,
communication and accountability.

2
00:00:10,519 --> 00:00:14,454
In this lesson, we'll see how the
platform keeps people informed,

3
00:00:14,464 --> 00:00:20,229
how SMS messages are sent, and how the
audit log keeps a lasting trail of actions.

4
00:00:22,185 --> 00:00:25,007
The platform communicates in two ways.

5
00:00:26,052 --> 00:00:29,141
In-app notifications
appear inside the platform,

6
00:00:29,151 --> 00:00:31,036
in the notification centre.

7
00:00:31,536 --> 00:00:36,884
Each one is addressed to a specific person, and
it's stored in the database until it's read.

8
00:00:37,919 --> 00:00:42,688
SMS messages are sent to mobile phones, so
people are informed even when they aren't

9
00:00:42,698 --> 00:00:43,798
signed in.

10
00:00:44,752 --> 00:00:49,189
Some events use both channels,
and some use SMS only.

11
00:00:49,689 --> 00:00:51,170
Let's look at each.

12
00:00:52,685 --> 00:00:58,293
Open Notifications from the sidebar, or
select the bell icon at the top of any page.

13
00:00:58,794 --> 00:01:02,658
When you have unread notifications,
the bell shows a count.

14
00:01:03,719 --> 00:01:07,003
Each notification has a
title, a short message,

15
00:01:07,013 --> 00:01:08,455
and when it arrived.

16
00:01:08,956 --> 00:01:13,262
Unread notifications are marked with
a green bar along the left edge.

17
00:01:14,319 --> 00:01:18,658
Here, the administrator has received
alerts for additional fund requests,

18
00:01:18,668 --> 00:01:20,878
and for submitted daily logs.

19
00:01:21,919 --> 00:01:26,434
Selecting a notification marks it as
read and opens the related project.

20
00:01:26,934 --> 00:01:30,525
You can also mark all your
notifications as read at once.

21
00:01:32,052 --> 00:01:35,225
Here's a map of the events
that trigger communication.

22
00:01:36,285 --> 00:01:39,634
When a team leader is created,
assigned to a project,

23
00:01:39,644 --> 00:01:42,486
or removed from one through
the project's edit form,

24
00:01:42,496 --> 00:01:44,445
they receive an SMS.

25
00:01:44,946 --> 00:01:48,171
The welcome message includes
their sign-in details.

26
00:01:49,219 --> 00:01:54,020
Direct messages from an administrator
arrive both in the app and by SMS.

27
00:01:55,052 --> 00:01:59,378
When a casual worker is added or removed,
the worker and the administrator are

28
00:01:59,388 --> 00:02:01,337
informed by SMS.

29
00:02:02,385 --> 00:02:06,125
When a team leader submits
a daily log, requests funds,

30
00:02:06,135 --> 00:02:12,186
or marks a project complete, the administrator
receives an in-app notification and an SMS.

31
00:02:13,219 --> 00:02:16,425
And when the administrator
approves or declines funds,

32
00:02:16,435 --> 00:02:21,471
or approves or returns a project, the
team leader is notified both ways.

33
00:02:23,119 --> 00:02:27,510
When an event triggers an SMS, the
platform prepares a short message,

34
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:31,110
and converts the phone number to
the international Kenyan format.

35
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:35,111
It then sends the message
to a Cloudflare Worker:

36
00:02:35,121 --> 00:02:40,664
a small, secure web service that sits
between the platform and the SMS provider.

37
00:02:41,719 --> 00:02:46,175
The Worker passes the message
to Mobilesasa, the SMS gateway,

38
00:02:46,185 --> 00:02:50,531
which delivers it to the recipient's
phone using the configured sender ID.

39
00:02:51,585 --> 00:02:55,872
If the phone number is missing or
invalid, or the service can't be reached,

40
00:02:55,882 --> 00:02:59,420
the message is marked as failed
rather than silently ignored.

41
00:03:00,919 --> 00:03:04,392
Administrators configure SMS under Settings.

42
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:09,414
The SMS Notifications panel shows
whether the system is in Live mode,

43
00:03:09,424 --> 00:03:10,996
or in Dry-run mode.

44
00:03:12,019 --> 00:03:15,486
The Worker URL is the address
of the Cloudflare Worker,

45
00:03:15,496 --> 00:03:19,450
and the Sender ID is the name that
appears on recipients' phones.

46
00:03:19,951 --> 00:03:22,030
These are technical settings.

47
00:03:22,529 --> 00:03:26,373
We've hidden the address here, and they
should only be changed on the advice of your

48
00:03:26,383 --> 00:03:27,695
technical team.

49
00:03:28,752 --> 00:03:31,678
Dry-run mode is a safe testing switch.

50
00:03:32,179 --> 00:03:36,335
When it's on, messages are recorded
in the platform's SMS list,

51
00:03:36,345 --> 00:03:38,217
but they're not actually sent.

52
00:03:39,619 --> 00:03:44,843
Under Auto-fire per event, each type of
automatic SMS can be switched on or off

53
00:03:44,853 --> 00:03:49,648
individually — for example, notifying
a team leader of a project assignment,

54
00:03:49,658 --> 00:03:52,754
or notifying the administrator
of each daily log.

55
00:03:53,819 --> 00:03:57,123
These switches control SMS messages only.

56
00:03:57,623 --> 00:04:00,419
In-app notifications are still created.

57
00:04:01,452 --> 00:04:06,260
One important detail: these SMS preferences
are saved in the web browser you're

58
00:04:06,270 --> 00:04:11,197
using. If an administrator signs
in on another computer or browser,

59
00:04:11,207 --> 00:04:13,768
the settings there need
to be checked separately.

60
00:04:14,819 --> 00:04:20,043
Below the switches, Save keeps your
changes to the Worker URL and Sender ID,

61
00:04:20,053 --> 00:04:24,685
and Test SMS sends a test message to
confirm that everything is working.

62
00:04:25,752 --> 00:04:29,700
The Recent SMS list then shows
each message's recipient,

63
00:04:29,710 --> 00:04:34,147
content and status:
sent, failed, or dry run.

64
00:04:34,647 --> 00:04:38,303
It covers messages sent from the
current browser session only.

65
00:04:39,719 --> 00:04:42,034
Now let's turn to accountability.

66
00:04:42,534 --> 00:04:47,433
The Audit Log, available to administrators,
records the important actions taken in

67
00:04:47,443 --> 00:04:48,543
the system.

68
00:04:49,519 --> 00:04:53,038
Each entry shows when the action
happened, who performed it,

69
00:04:53,048 --> 00:04:56,866
what the action was, and the
details — such as an amount,

70
00:04:56,876 --> 00:04:58,943
a project, or a person.

71
00:04:59,985 --> 00:05:04,285
Here, we can see an expense being
added, a project being created,

72
00:05:04,295 --> 00:05:07,840
funds being requested and
approved, a daily log submitted,

73
00:05:07,850 --> 00:05:09,826
and a casual worker added.

74
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:14,416
Entries are written automatically
as people use the system.

75
00:05:14,917 --> 00:05:18,123
There's no option in the
platform to edit or delete them,

76
00:05:18,133 --> 00:05:21,410
and the page shows the most
recent one hundred entries.

77
00:05:22,452 --> 00:05:27,670
The dashboard's Recent Activity panel shows
the latest six entries from the same log.

78
00:05:29,219 --> 00:05:33,981
It's worth being clear about the difference
between a notification and an audit record.

79
00:05:35,019 --> 00:05:38,401
A notification is a message
to a specific person.

80
00:05:38,901 --> 00:05:42,921
Its purpose is to prompt action:
something needs your attention.

81
00:05:43,420 --> 00:05:46,164
Once it's read, its job is done.

82
00:05:47,219 --> 00:05:50,900
An audit record is a lasting
entry in the system's history.

83
00:05:51,401 --> 00:05:54,763
Its purpose is accountability:
it shows who did what,

84
00:05:54,773 --> 00:05:57,778
and when, so the record
can be reviewed later.

85
00:05:58,819 --> 00:06:02,689
Together, they make sure that the right
people are informed in the moment,

86
00:06:02,699 --> 00:06:06,849
and that the organisation can always
reconstruct what happened afterwards.

87
00:06:08,685 --> 00:06:14,704
To recap: in-app notifications prompt
action, SMS reaches people wherever they are,

88
00:06:14,714 --> 00:06:17,393
and the audit log keeps a lasting record.

89
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:22,836
Administrators can control which automatic
SMS messages are sent and test the

90
00:06:22,846 --> 00:06:26,391
service safely, and everyone
should keep phone numbers accurate,

91
00:06:26,401 --> 00:06:28,871
so that messages reach the right people.

92
00:06:29,919 --> 00:06:34,232
In the final lesson, we'll bring everything
together with system administration,

93
00:06:34,242 --> 00:06:37,650
the platform's architecture,
and best practices.

94
00:06:40,619 --> 00:06:44,639
This training experience was
produced by KEYPOLE TECHNOLOGIES.
